Goal
Resolve parameter name conflicts with the pre-configured `--help` option by 
automatically renaming its internal storage identifier when a user-defined 
parameter named `help` is present.

Files to modify
  • src/click/core.py
  • src/click/parser.py
  • tests/test_commands.py

Implementation steps
  1. Step 1: In `src/click/core.py`, modify the logic that creates or retrieves 
the default `--help` option (likely within `Command.get_help_option()` or the 
`Command.__init__` where the option is added) so that if a user parameter 
already claims the name 'help', the help option's internal name is changed to a 
non-conflicting variant by appending underscores until unique (e.g., 'help_', 
'help__').
  2. Step 2: In `src/click/parser.py`, verify that `OptionParser.add_option()` 
(or equivalent option registration logic) gracefully accepts the remapped dest 
string from Step 1 without overwriting or conflicting with the user-defined 
parameter of the same base name.
  3. Step 3: In `tests/test_commands.py`, add a test case that creates a command
with a user-defined `@click.option('--help', ...)` or `@click.argument('help')`,
invokes the parser with that parameter, and separately asserts that invoking 
`--help` still displays the help text and exits cleanly.
  4. Step 4: Run the test suite to confirm that the built-in help mechanism and 
the user-defined `help` parameter coexist without exceptions.

Tests to run
  $ pytest tests/test_commands.py
  $ pytest tests/test_parser.py

Risks
  ⚠  Hard-coding the underscore-suffix convention may conflict with existing 
parameters that already use underscore-padded names.
  ⚠  Changing the internal parameter name could break custom callback logic or 
subclass overrides that expect the built-in help option's name to be exactly 
'help'.

